  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Project Scope**\n\nOkay, I\'m getting a clearer picture. It seems the core goal is a web app, a ticketing and promotion platform. The \"Nocturnal Elegance\" design system, with its deep charcoal and electric violet, is the aesthetic foundation. I\'m focusing on parsing the input elements and developing a feature list that I can use to map out some rough plans for the front end and backend!\n\n\n**Revising Feature Prioritization**\n\nI\'ve refined the feature set further, focusing on core client-side functionality. The initial requests were straightforward; dynamic image linking is key. I\'m prioritizing interactive mock data and a simulated ticketing checkout. I\'m omitting both the Gemini AI and Firebase integration unless these are explicitly requested for future expansion, based on our earlier decisions and user requirements.\n\n\n**Expanding Feature Mapping**\n\nI\'m now focusing on integrating the promoter dashboard and event creation features. Analyzing the provided screens reveals key design elements: a \"Thiesdn Billetterie\" logo, distinct category pills, and featured event carousels. I\'m prioritizing the implementation of these components, alongside incorporating the WebGL background toggle or glassmorphism aesthetic to meet the initial design specifications.\n\n\n**Developing User Account Flows**\n\nI\'m now implementing the user account features, starting with authentication. The \"Connexion\" screen includes a dark diamond backdrop and a Thiesdn logo. The design is elegant, with interactive login options and a \"Continue with Google\" feature, with the option to register. I\'m also planning quick demo logins for different user types. After login, the user profile shows a \"Bento\" header with avatar and VIP badge. I\'m incorporating user data management, including editable personal information and connected account toggles!\n\n\n**Implementing Event Creation**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the event creation flow within the promoter hub. I\'m building out the \"Cr\303\251er un \303\211v\303\251nement\" screen, including navigation and submission handling. I\'m focusing on the input fields for the event title, category selection, start and end times, location with a map pin trigger for Dakar, Paris, Abidjan and Montreal, event poster upload, YouTube URL integration, pricing, and WhatsApp contact details. I will ensure that submitting an event sends it to the moderation queue. I\'m prioritizing user privacy with public profile controls, biometric login options, and notification settings. I also aim to include a \"My Tickets\" view with a QR code scanner and event countdown functionality, along with a secure sign-out option.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 4
      nanos: 696859414
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
